From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: count received data frames in the interface statistics

On a station the interface's rx counters do not follow the
data it receives, so `ip -s link`, /sys/class/net/<if>/statistics and
anything built on them (NetworkManager, monitoring, a check that traffic
used the radio) see a receive path that carries nothing. Measured on the
6 GiB board, 2026-09-23: two iperf3 -R runs
received 95.1 MB and 137 MB over the radio, and rx_bytes went from 2530
to 2791 (rx_packets 14 -> 17) while tx_bytes followed the sent data. The previous pin showed the same
on 2026-08-14 ("they barely move under load", out-of-tree/aic8800/README.md).

In the vendor driver: rwnx_rx_data_skb() updates
net_stats.rx_packets and net_stats.rx_bytes inside
`#ifdef CONFIG_BR_SUPPORT` (rwnx_rx.c:581-609 in the pinned tag, the
counters at :586-587), the NAT2.5 bridge block. CONFIG_BR_SUPPORT is n
(aic8800_fdrv/Makefile:81), so the two lines are not compiled and every
frame this function hands to the stack goes up uncounted. The vendor's
SDIO and PCIe copies of the same function in the same tag count after the
`#endif`: src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c:682-683,
src/PCIE/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c:589-590,
src/PCIE/driver_fw/driver/aic8800d80x2/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c:591-592.
The USB copy has them inside, and so do the older USB board ports under
src/USB/patch/ that carry the bridge block. The tx side has no such guard:
rwnx_tx_push() and rwnx_txdatacfm() count unconditionally (rwnx_tx.c:667,
:704, :2437), which is why only rx is flat.

Which frames that is, by reading rwnx_rxdataind_aicwf() (rwnx_rx.c:2223;
this build defines AICWF_RX_REORDER):
- station and P2P client (:2746): QoS frames the firmware marks
  flags_need_reord go to reord_process_unit() -> reord_single_frame_ind(),
  which counts (:1749-1750). QoS frames without flags_need_reord (:2761)
  and non-QoS frames (:2764) go to rwnx_rx_data_skb() and were not
  counted.
- AP and P2P GO (:2767): rwnx_rx_data_skb_forward() counts (:394-395), and
  the AP reorder path ends in reord_single_frame_ind() as well. Untouched.
- reassembled fragments, any interface type (:2683): rwnx_rx_data_skb(),
  not counted.
- management frames (:2703) go to cfg80211 and never reach net_stats.
So a flat counter needs the radio to be a station, and the few frames
unpatched driver did count took the reorder path. Which frames those were was not
read on the board.

What changes: the two lines move below the `#endif`, where the SDIO and
PCIe copies have them, with a comment that says why they are there. Same
counter, same value: skb->len of the 802.3 frame before eth_type_trans(),
as reord_single_frame_ind() and rwnx_rx_data_skb_forward() in this driver
count it. Each frame leaves through exactly one of the three functions, so
nothing is counted twice. rwnx_get_stats() returns these fields through
.ndo_get_stats (rwnx_main.c:1746-1751, :1794, :1817), and
rwnx_fill_station_info() reports the same two as the station's rx
counters (rwnx_main.c:5753, :5756).

How mainline does it, read in linux-6.18.53:
- include/uapi/linux/if_link.h:56-59: rx_bytes is "the length of Ethernet
  Frames excluding the FCS" -- the header included, so counted before
  eth_type_trans() pulls it.
- mac80211, ieee80211_deliver_skb(): dev_sw_netstats_rx_add(dev,
  skb->len) at net/mac80211/rx.c:2690, eth_type_trans() at :2761.
- mwifiex, a cfg80211 FullMAC driver of the same shape as this one (a
  private struct net_device_stats returned through .ndo_get_stats,
  drivers/net/wireless/marvell/mwifiex/main.c:1279, :1302):
  mwifiex_recv_packet() counts at util.c:534-535, eth_type_trans() at :548.
This patch counts where mwifiex does, once per frame on the way to the
stack.

Not done here: the counters stay plain `unsigned long` increments, as at
every other counting site in this driver. The busrx thread and
reord_timeout_worker() (rwnx_rx.c:1901, a work item) count the same fields,
so a rare lost increment under concurrency is possible, as it already was
on the reorder path. Per-CPU counters (dev_sw_netstats_rx_add(), as
mac80211) would have to replace every counting site at once -- tx
included -- or the counters would live in two mechanisms; that is a change
of its own. rx_dropped for frames this path frees, and the multicast
counter, are left as the vendor has them.

Origin: the same move was proposed once before and dropped unrun. This patch
re-derives it against the pinned tag and adds the reading above.

Falsifier, on the board, radio as station on a link that exists only on
the radio (one board as station, a peer as access point and iperf3 server), read
/sys/class/net/<if>/statistics before and after one `iperf3 -R` run with
no omitted seconds:
1. With this patch the rx_bytes delta is at least iperf3's receiver byte
   count and at most ~10 % above it: a full TCP segment carries 1448 bytes
   of payload in a 1514-byte Ethernet frame (~5 %). Without it the delta
   stays far below the transfer (+261 B for 137 MB measured); frames that take
   the reorder path are counted either way. rx_packets moves with it.
2. The same with the radio as AP: the delta must match the transfer as
   before and must not double; that path is not touched.
3. WLAN associates and passes traffic as before.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
index 5085465..2664bb6 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
@@ -581,11 +581,6 @@ static bool rwnx_rx_data_skb(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw, struct rwnx_vif *rwnx_vif,
 #ifdef CONFIG_BR_SUPPORT
             void *br_port = NULL;
 
-
-            /* Update statistics */
-            rwnx_vif->net_stats.rx_packets++;
-            rwnx_vif->net_stats.rx_bytes += rx_skb->len;
-
             if (1) {//(check_fwstate(pmlmepriv, WIFI_STATION_STATE | WIFI_ADHOC_STATE) == _TRUE) {
                 /* Insert NAT2.5 RX here! */
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE <= KERNEL_VERSION(2, 6, 35))
@@ -608,6 +603,12 @@ static bool rwnx_rx_data_skb(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw, struct rwnx_vif *rwnx_vif,
             }
 #endif /* CONFIG_BR_SUPPORT */
 
+            /* Update statistics. Outside CONFIG_BR_SUPPORT, where the
+             * vendor's SDIO and PCIe copies of this function count: inside
+             * it, a build without the bridge counted none of these frames. */
+            rwnx_vif->net_stats.rx_packets++;
+            rwnx_vif->net_stats.rx_bytes += rx_skb->len;
+
 		rwnx_skb_align_8bytes(rx_skb);
 
         rx_skb->protocol = eth_type_trans(rx_skb, rwnx_vif->ndev);
